  "comparison": "Compare upward transcript movement for five keyboard-only modal hosts, batched extension input, an empty selector and a mouse-aware selector. PiSharp invokes real dialogs/progress/search under a PTY; Pi invokes TuiAltScreen/VirtualTerminal with focused mouse-aware and unaware components. Typed text and selection/progress outcomes are asserted in PiSharp, and wheel never reaches Pi keyboard input. Full cell layout, pointer selection, selector movement increments, keyboard viewport key handling and non-POSIX hosts are not covered."
